'''''Marchantia paleacea''''' is a species of [[Marchantiophyta|liverwort]] found in North America, Europe, and eastern Asia. It has been employed as a model organism to study plant-fungal symbioses.<ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Humphreys |first1=Claire P. |last2=Franks |first2=Peter J. |last3=Rees |first3=Mark |last4=Bidartondo |first4=Martin I. |last5=Leake |first5=Jonathan R. |last6=Beerling |first6=David J. |date=2010-11-02 |title=Mutualistic mycorrhiza-like symbiosis in the most ancient group of land plants |url=https://www.nature.com/articles/ncomms1105 |journal=Nature Communications |language=en |volume=1 |issue=1 |pages=103 |doi=10.1038/ncomms1105  |doi-access=free|pmid=21045821 |bibcode=2010NatCo...1..103H |issn=2041-1723}}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal |last1=Kodama |first1=Kyoichi |last2=Rich |first2=Mélanie K. |last3=Yoda |first3=Akiyoshi |last4=Shimazaki |first4=Shota |last5=Xie |first5=Xiaonan |last6=Akiyama |first6=Kohki |last7=Mizuno |first7=Yohei |last8=Komatsu |first8=Aino |last9=Luo |first9=Yi |last10=Suzuki |first10=Hidemasa |last11=Kameoka |first11=Hiromu |last12=Libourel |first12=Cyril |last13=Keller |first13=Jean |last14=Sakakibara |first14=Keiko |last15=Nishiyama |first15=Tomoaki |date=2022-07-08 |title=An ancestral function of strigolactones as symbiotic rhizosphere signals |journal=Nature Communications |language=en |volume=13 |issue=1 |pages=3974 |doi=10.1038/s41467-022-31708-3  |doi-access=free|issn=2041-1723 |pmc=9270392 |pmid=35803942 |bibcode=2022NatCo..13.3974K}}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal |last=Bouwmeester |first=Harro J. |date=2021-05-21 |title=Plant lipids enticed fungi to mutualism |url=https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.abi8016 |journal=Science |language=en |volume=372 |issue=6544 |pages=789–790 |doi=10.1126/science.abi8016 |pmid=34016767 |bibcode=2021Sci...372..789B |s2cid=234794567 |issn=0036-8075|hdl=11245.1/de4f258f-23fb-4fce-8831-51aed8287cb3 |hdl-access=free }}</ref>

